<title>MEXICO: U.S.-Mexico satellite deal hindered, says company.</title>
<headline>U.S.-Mexico satellite deal hindered, says company.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negotiations on a reciprocal communications agreement between Mexico and the United States has been hindered by Mexico's lack of a satellite whose footprint covers the United States, a Mexican communications company president said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Mexico does not have a satellite whose footprint covers the United States at present, and as long as this is the case, it is very difficult to allow U.S. satellite signals to enter Mexico,&quot; Medcom president Clemente Serna said in an interview.</p>
<p>Medcom, S.A. de C.V. is one of four Mexican companies awaiting the inking of U.S.-Mexico protocols to begin direct-to-home television services in Mexico.</p>
<p>-- Claudia Villegas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9549</p>
</text>
